WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.720
<b>The World's Supreme Authority</b>

3
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.370
You got somethin' you wanna
say to me, you little brat?

4
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.610
Well, speak up!

5
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.540
I do. Give back Pops'
gold! Every bit of it!

6
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.780
What gold?

7
00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.570
You mean the junk we got
from old man Cricket?

8
00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:25.540
Maybe it's news to you,

9
00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.780
but that's what pirates do.

10
00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.460
Ever heard of looting?

11
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.530
But what am I saying?

12
00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.200
You're just a pathetic dreamer

13
00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.670
who can't open his
eyes long enough

14
00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.730
to get a good look
at the real world.

15
00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.370
Well, then.

16
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.570
If stealing is just
what we pirates do,

17
00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.340
I guess I should steal
the gold back then.

18
00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:49.750
"100 Million Man!

19
00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.500
That's cute. But be serious,
can you really fight?

20
00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.040
I mean, do you even know
how to throw a punch?

21
00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.680
I saw your
fighting skills earlier.

22
00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.610
You're very good at
just standing there.

23
00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.620
I... I was right.

24
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.520
That's him.

25
00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.220
You're still hangin'
on to that thing?

26
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.110
Didn't you hear?
It's worthless. Get rid of it.

27
00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.310
But if this is the real thing,
then Bellamy's in trouble.

28
00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.640
He's good, but you have to
admit, he can't beat someone

29
00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.650
with a hundred‐
million‐Berry bounty.

30
00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.520
You've gotta be joking.

31
00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.060
Look at him. He's
just a little runt.

32
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.530
He's probably not even
worth the trouble

33
00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.020
it would take to fight him.

34
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.570
Just seeing him now
makes me doubt

35
00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:30.370
that 30‐million‐Berry bounty.

36
00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.650
Standing there isn't
gonna get the gold back.

37
00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.360
What? You freezing up
like this afternoon?

38
00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.660
Admit it: You're too
scared to fight me.

39
00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.410
This afternoon was
different. I'm not scared.

40
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.100
We'll see about that
real soon, Straw Hat.

41
00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.980
I'm sick of listening to you,

42
00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:50.210
so I think I'll shut you
up for good this time.

43
00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.130
It's collapsing!

44
00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.300
Don't worry, this
won't take long.

45
00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.520
Spring Sniper!

46
00:03:58.550 --> 00:03:59.960
Haa!

47
00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.690
You're nothing but a little boy
who still believes in dreams.

48
00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.560
You disgrace the rest of us
by calling yourself a pirate.

49
00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:16.260
It's time to stop this foolish
dreaming and grow up.

50
00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.830
Now let's end this!

51
00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.700
He's headed right for us!

52
00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:22.970
Run!

53
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.650
Looks like your dreams
are at an end.

54
00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.300
He's alive!

55
00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:39.930
You don't know when
to quit, do you?!

56
00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.300
Fine! Have it your way!

57
00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.640
We're just getting
to the good part!

58
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.670
Spring... Hopper!

59
00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.110
Bellamy disappeared!

60
00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.330
This is the same kinda move
he pulled to beat Roshio.

61
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.020
So you want the gold back, huh?

62
00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.860
Because old man
Cricket's your friend?

63
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.070
Wake up!

64
00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.240
He's nothing but a decrepit fool

65
00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.910
who spends all his time chasing
after a 400‐year‐old lie.

66
00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.210
But that's probably what
you like about him, right?

67
00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.250
You like to call yourselves
pirates, but you know nothing.

68
00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.050
There's no city of gold,
no island in the sky.

69
00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.160
Just oceans and ships
and the men who sail them.

70
00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:25.060
You asked if I know
how to throw a punch.

71
00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.430
Just finish him so we
can drink, Bellamy.

72
00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.870
Watching you beat him
senseless has made me thirsty.

73
00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.810
So long, Straw Hat!

74
00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.420
Whoa.

75
00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.490
Hey, quit messing around,
Bellamy, and get up.

76
00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:15.390
The joke's over. We know that
runt couldn't beat you.

77
00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.290
C'mon, get up!

78
00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.910
This really isn't funny
anymore! Now snap out of it.

79
00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.990
You have to get up and
show that kid who you are.

80
00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.000
You're a real pirate,
not like him.

81
00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:32.330
Your bounty's up to 55 million...
you can't lose to some rookie!

82
00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.940
Those two together
are worth 160 million!

83
00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:41.940
Their bounties are
higher than yours, Bellamy!

84
00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.840
Know what that means?
You're dead meat!

85
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.230
You see now? I told
you it was true.

86
00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:54.820
And now, Cricket's gold.
Give it back.

87
00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.490
– Fix the ship, Monkey Crew, fix the ship.
– Fix the ship, Monkey Crew, fix the ship.

88
00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:08.800
– Bang the nails, Monkey Crew, bang the nails.
– Bang the nails, Monkey Crew, bang the nails.

89
00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.260
– Saw the wood, Monkey Crew, saw the wood.
– Saw the wood, Monkey Crew, saw the wood.

90
00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.290
Wow, these guys are
must be pretty tough.

91
00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.490
They were just beaten
unconscious

92
00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:17.800
and now they're here
fixing the ship.

93
00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.430
Either they're the
world's fastest healers

94
00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:22.130
or Chopper's the
world's best doctor.

95
00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.270
Why didn't you go with Luffy?

96
00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.010
What? What's with you?

97
00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:31.210
Fight, don't fight. Go, don't
go. Do this, no do that.

98
00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:32.580
Make up your mind already!

99
00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:33.550
Heh. You're scared!

100
00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.960
Those guys beat you
the first time around.

101
00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.400
That's what you think?

102
00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.270
You don't get it.
They didn't beat us.

103
00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.370
Refusing to fight doesn't
mean that we were afraid.

104
00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.900
When there's no reason to fight,

105
00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.290
the only way to win
is to stand down.

106
00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.860
Oh, I see. "Stand
down." Real brave.

107
00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.330
You don't know anything about
fighting! Just shut up!

108
00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.270
Don't tell me to shut up!

109
00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:54.770
Like it matters.
You never listen anyway!

110
00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:55.640
I know more...

111
00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:57.810
Guys, come on. Be careful!

112
00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.240
Yeah! Be more
careful with the ship!

113
00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.280
We're trying to fix
the ship, not destroy it.

114
00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:05.820
Hey. Seriously! Oh, c'mon!

115
00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.290
That wasn't too hard to find.

116
00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.180
It‐It's not possible.

117
00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.720
How could we lose?

118
00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.350
Hey you, come back here!

119
00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.790
You hear me?!

120
00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:23.960
You stupid runt!
I'm talking to you!

121
00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:27.290
I'll get him! We won't be
beaten by some pretend pirate!

122
00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.400
I'll show you a real punch!
Where are you going?

123
00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.670
Where am I going?

124
00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:39.420
Up there.

125
00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:54.140
<b>The Previous Afternoon
An Island in the Grand Line</b>

126
00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.860
Captain. Captain!

127
00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.910
What?!

128
00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:04.540
Is... Is this really the place?

129
00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:08.080
The legendary cave place where
Captain John hid his treasure.

130
00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:12.110
The treasure he killed
so many innocents to get?

131
00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.620
Yes. That's right.

132
00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:15.750
Now look alive boys,

133
00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.710
the treasure is near but
so is unspeakable danger.

134
00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:20.840
If you let your guard
down even for a second,

135
00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.670
then death will creep on you.

136
00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.480
There's no telling what
kind of monsters will appear

137
00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.550
or what vicious booby traps
await to kill us all.

138
00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:32.820
C'mon, men!

139
00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:35.780
Another fine day of
carving out tunnels awaits us!

140
00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:36.780
– Right‐O, Boss!
– Right‐O, Boss!

141
00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:40.310
"Boss"

142
00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.600
Oh. You must be the new
guys they sent down.

143
00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.800
Nothing like working
up a sweat, right, Boss?

144
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.800
All a man really needs
is a pick axe in his hand

145
00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.190
and a tunnel to dig!

146
00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:54.910
"Boss"

147
00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.610
You can say that again!

148
00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.190
A hard days work
is a wonderful thing!

149
00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.350
And because of our good
old‐fashioned elbow grease,

150
00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:55.600
everyone who comes
to this tunnel will smile!

151
00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:57.100
It's liberating!

152
00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.770
You know,
after all this hard labor,

153
00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.690
we outta head to the
Ol' Bilge Barge for a...

154
00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:06.650
How dare you make me
work like one of your lackies!

155
00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.090
Not one single piece of treasure
on that whole rotten island.

156
00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:21.720
You know, you should really
watch what you say Mohji!

157
00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.470
If there's one thing the
captain hates, it's being wrong.

158
00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.520
I mean, can't you see
how red he's gotten

159
00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:27.890
with all the embarrassment?

160
00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:31.190
Who's nose is a
big red embarrassment?

161
00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:35.270
I hate to interrupt.

162
00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:37.110
But we do not
have time for this.

163
00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:39.960
What are we going to
do about those Straw Hats?

164
00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:42.130
They are quickly becoming
the new favorite pirates

165
00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.510
in the Grand Line.

166
00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:44.780
I have a plan of course.

167
00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:45.630
You moron!

168
00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.510
We let 'em go
on their merry way.

169
00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:49.930
What? Why?

170
00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:52.120
Well, you see, before
an evil witch feasts

171
00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.370
upon the flesh of children
the first thing the she does

172
00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:56.200
is makes sure to fatten them up.

173
00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:58.020
Understand me?

174
00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:00.070
Idiots.

175
00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.130
This is why I'm Captain.

176
00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:04.000
See, the bigger the bounty
gets on the Straw Hats...

177
00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:04.760
I see!

178
00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:05.560
You're a genius, Captain!

179
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.310
That way when
you take them down,

180
00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.800
the bounty on your
head will get even higher.

181
00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:15.360
Yes! Exactly!

182
00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.140
You're amazing, Captain!

183
00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:19.300
Shall we throw a party
in honor of your brilliance?

184
00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:21.000
Oh, why not?

185
00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.330
Is this really
the time to be throwing a party?

186
00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:26.820
After all, how can you plan on

187
00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.250
beating Luffy
and the Straw Hat's

188
00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.670
when you haven't the faintest
idea of where they are?

189
00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.780
Don't be such a
party pooper, Alvida.

190
00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:34.660
We'll find Luffy
when we find him.

191
00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.080
Okay?

192
00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.740
If you're looking for Luffy,

193
00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:39.680
I can tell you where he is.

194
00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:40.870
Ha! You see?

195
00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:43.040
This guy over here is going
to tell us where he is.

196
00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.900
Problem solved!

197
00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:48.200
Hey! Hold on! Who are you?

198
00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:49.410
Sorry for crashing your party,

199
00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.810
but I simply couldn't resist the
delicious aromas of your feast.

200
00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:54.650
My name is Portgas D. Ace.

201
00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:56.040
But you can call me Ace.

202
00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.070
Oh, no need to be so formal.

203
00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.410
Nice to meet you too!

204
00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.330
I mean, what are you
doing here, you idiot?!

205
00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.370
I couldn't care less
about what your name is,

206
00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.080
Mr. Portgas D. Ace!

207
00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.580
Uh, Captain.

208
00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:12.610
Captain, this guy is...

209
00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.210
He's the Fire Fist.

210
00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:15.590
Fire Fist Ace!

211
00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.960
Captain of the Whitebeard
Pirates Second Unit!

212
00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:21.150
Not Whitebeard's...?!

213
00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.930
Ah! So you know the old man?

214
00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.090
What a nice...

215
00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:27.350
He fell asleep?

216
00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:30.380
No, I won't!

217
00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:31.370
Why not?

218
00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:32.550
Captain, this could
be our only chance.

219
00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:35.750
If we can take out Fire Fist
Ace of the Whitebeard Pirates,

220
00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:37.290
we'll be famous!

221
00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.170
I said no!

222
00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.070
Remember this, men,
and remember it good.

223
00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.860
This is the most important
lesson you'll ever learn:

224
00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:48.200
Don't mess with
the Whitebeard Pirates.

225
00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.030
Ever!

226
00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:51.610
Whitebeard is a
killer born and bred.

227
00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.200
The only man who could go

228
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:56.620
toe‐to‐toe with Gold Roger,
the King of the Pirates.

229
00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.330
He is without a doubt
the strongest pirate alive

230
00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:00.500
and the person closest

231
00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:04.170
to obtaining the greatest
treasure of all, One Piece!

232
00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:07.150
In other words, don't cross him!

233
00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:10.690
Even if we were able to kill
Fire Fist Ace while he sleeps,

234
00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:12.820
Whitebeard would avenge
the murder of one of his own

235
00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:15.060
with the fury
of a thunderstrorm!

236
00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.570
How is it that you know so much?

237
00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:18.610
Pray tell.

238
00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.740
Well, if you insist.

239
00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.410
It was on the Grand Line.

240
00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:25.660
Years ago.

241
00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:29.040
I met that man face to face, and
I've never been the same since.

242
00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:32.690
Sorry about that.
I must've dozed off.

243
00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:34.860
What the? He's awake?

244
00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:40.610
Hey, hey! Why the long faces, everyone?
I thought this was a party? Am I right?

245
00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:41.990
Oh, yeah, you're right.

246
00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:44.870
Men, commence having fun again!

247
00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.350
Ace, you sure know how
to have a good time!

248
00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.290
Whoa! You guys got a lion?

249
00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.830
Be a good kitty and jump through
that flaming hoop on two legs.

250
00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:56.000
C'mon, Rich!

251
00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.340
Show him your stuff!

252
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.370
<b>The Holy Land, Mary Geoise</b>

253
00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.370
Red Hair and Whitebeard?

254
00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:25.970
"Justice"

255
00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:22.170
Yes. Red Hair made contact.

256
00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.770
That is disturbing.

257
00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.010
I assume he didn't go himself?

258
00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:28.040
No. He sent one of his crew.

259
00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.600
Elder, I'm concerned.

260
00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:31.910
These two working together
could mean real trouble

261
00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:32.640
for the rest of us.

262
00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:46.410
<b>The Five Elders
Supreme Council of
the World Government</b>

263
00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.200
Yes, but let's wait for now.

264
00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:36.580
They haven't done anything yet,

265
00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:40.150
and Red Hair isn't the type
to act unless he's provoked.

266
00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.220
We'll keep an eye on them,

267
00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:44.270
but I'm afraid we have more
pressing worries to tend to.

268
00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.800
We need to focus on
the Seven Warlords.

269
00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:49.710
With Crocodile gone, we are
in need of a replacement.

270
00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.980
Pirates they may be, the
Warlords keep things balanced.

271
00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:54.740
With one of their number gone,

272
00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.950
we may encounter
serious problems.

273
00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.050
What plans have we made so far?

274
00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.280
Sir!

275
00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:03.030
We've called all of the Warlords
to Marie Jois for a meeting,

276
00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.840
but there's no way to know
how many of them will

277
00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.200
actually show up.

278
00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:09.140
They are pirates, after all.
They do as they please.

279
00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.470
Dammit, Crocodile.

280
00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:13.370
It's because of you
that we're in this mess.

281
00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.840
We can't let the pirates that
defeated him go unpunished.

282
00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:18.950
We have to retaliate swiftly.

283
00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:21.610
I want all of our energy
concentrated on finding

284
00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:24.080
this Monkey D. Luffy.

285
00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.980
Navy
Headquarters to Marie Jois:

286
00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:31.850
Announcing the arrival
of Warlords

287
00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:35.320
Donquixote Doflamingo
and Bartholomew Kuma.

288
00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.540
<b>Donquixote Doflamingo
Warlord of the Sea
Former Bounty: 340 Million Belly</b>

289
00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:42.500
<b>Bartholomew Kuma
Warlord of the Sea
Former Bounty: 296 Million Belly</b>

290
00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.310
What the...? Hey, stop it.

291
00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:50.010
What are you doing?

292
00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.140
It's not me! I don't
know what's going on.

293
00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:54.350
This isn't the time
for your stupid pranks.

294
00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.630
It's no prank.

295
00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:57.700
It's like something's moving my
hands and I can't stop them.

296
00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.830
That's ridiculous.
I can't breathe!

297
00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:01.700
Stop it! What
the devil are you fools doing?

298
00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.240
Are you trying to kill me?

299
00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.130
Look, I told you, it's not me!

300
00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:08.900
Get off me!

301
00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.910
<b>"Master Tactician" Tsuru
Vice Admiral, Navy HQ</b>

302
00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:10.570
This is your doing!

303
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.500
Do you find this
entertaining, Doflamingo?

304
00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.240
Hm. Yes, actually.

305
00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:19.040
If you don't mind, I'd like to
get this little shindig started

306
00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:21.310
sometime in the near future.

307
00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.310
Unless you haven't had enough.

308
00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:30.050
"Justice"

309
00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:28.990
You idiot!

310
00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:30.030
What do you think
you're doing now?

311
00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:31.330
This foolishness has gone on

312
00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:33.180
long enough, Doflamingo!

313
00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.060
Stop! Enough!

314
00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.270
There's no time for this.

315
00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:39.970
Now sit down. There are
pressing matters to discuss.

316
00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:43.070
<b>Sengoku "the Buddha"
Fleet Admiral, Navy HQ
(Naval Commander in Chief)</b>

317
00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.650
I apologize for
the late welcome.

318
00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:53.020
Thank you for coming,
scum of the sea.

319
00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:54.220
Thank you.

320
00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:57.710
So thoughtful of you, using
my formal title like that.

321
00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:58.680
Let's begin.

322
00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:02.220
I doubt any more of the
Warlords plan to attend.

323
00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:05.510
Truth be told, two out of six
is more than I expected.

324
00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:06.640
Smart man.

325
00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:07.650
I didn't plan to come either,

326
00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.760
but the business back
home's going so well,

327
00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:14.730
it practically runs itself,
so I took a vacation.

328
00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.270
Ended up here out
of sheer boredom.

329
00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.190
Forgive me for not applauding
your business success.

330
00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:21.660
I'm afraid that,
for the rest of us,

331
00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.460
there are few things
more distressing

332
00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.730
than a booming pirate industry.

333
00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:30.570
While I admire a man who's
not afraid to speak his mind,

334
00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:34.570
I would remember, Admiral,
that there are limits.

335
00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:42.020
So good to hear your
dulcet tones again, Doflamingo.

336
00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:45.190
And you, Admiral Sengoku,
I hope you've been well.

337
00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:46.690
Hawk‐Eye!

338
00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.430
I must say,
I've never understood

339
00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.300
why the Seven Warlords
and the Marines

340
00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.200
insist on pretending
they get along,

341
00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:53.930
but perhaps you
can enlighten me.

342
00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.200
Hawk‐Eye Mihawk.

343
00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:58.670
Perhaps this little get‐together
will be interesting after all.

344
00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.640
What brings you here, Mihawk?

345
00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:02.670
Well, I heard about your meeting

346
00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.510
and thought I might
sit in on it.

347
00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.760
I have an interest in the
pirates you'll be discussing,

348
00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.610
and I'd like to stay informed.

349
00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.650
That is all.

350
00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:13.350
Forgive the intrusion,
but if Hawk‐Eye's staying,

351
00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:16.510
perhaps you won't mind adding
one more to the party.

352
00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.580
I will tell you though,

353
00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:21.080
my intentions are a bit
less passive than his are.

354
00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:22.820
Who are you, exactly?

355
00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:25.320
And how'd you get
in here anyway?

356
00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:30.350
Quite a prestigious group you've assembled
here, Admiral. I'm truly impressed.

357
00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.650
I was hoping I might join you.

358
00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:36.020
Huh?

359
00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.760
I heard the
news about Crocodile.

360
00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.130
It's a terrible shame he's gone.

361
00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.610
Fortunately for you, I've come
here to offer a solution

362
00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.240
to your little problem.

363
00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.710
"The Six Warlords"
just doesn't have

364
00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:54.090
the same ring to it, does it?

365
00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:57.120
I know him! That man's Laffitte!

366
00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.110
Who's Laffitte?

367
00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:01.360
Ah‐ha. Someone here has
heard my name before.

368
00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:03.530
I'd have thought it
had been forgotten.

369
00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:06.110
A long time ago, he was
a respected peace officer

370
00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:07.240
in the West Blue Sea.

371
00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:10.680
He disappeared after a scandal
ruined his reputation.

372
00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:13.710
Glad to see
you're so well‐informed.

373
00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:17.210
Who I am doesn't matter.
All that's in the past.

374
00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:19.310
I've come here to talk to
you about another man.

375
00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:20.240
One who I believe would make

376
00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:23.340
an excellent addition
to the Warlords.

377
00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:29.690
<b>The Grand Line</b>

378
00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:25.820
Shanks.

379
00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:29.180
I haven't heard that
name in a long time.

380
00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:33.520
So, after all these years,
he's sent me a letter?

381
00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.490
Yeah, and whatever it
says must be important

382
00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.090
or else he wouldn't have chosen
me to deliver it for him.

383
00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.130
I see. You're high
up on the food chain, are you?

384
00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:42.280
Well, uh, not exactly.

385
00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.490
I mean I am still new
to the Red‐Haired Pirates...

386
00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:46.620
<b>Rockstar
Red Hair Pirates (Newcomer)
Bounty: 94 Million Belly</b>

387
00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:49.220
But it's not like this
is my first pirate gig.

388
00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.220
I've been around for a while,

389
00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:53.520
and I'm pretty sure I've
made a name for myself.

390
00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:54.690
Hey, you guys have heard about

391
00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.460
that famous pirate
named Rockstar, right?

392
00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:59.760
Uh‐uh. I've never
heard of him before.

393
00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.320
Hey! What are you...?

394
00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:09.660
He sent me a letter?

395
00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.690
When did that kid
become so important

396
00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.330
that he thought it would be
okay to send me a letter?

397
00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.600
Time to take him down a notch.

398
00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:19.330
Wait! Hold on!

399
00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:23.440
What do you think you're doing?
That was an important letter.

400
00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.150
This is Shanks you're
dealing with...

401
00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:27.330
the leader of the
Red‐Haired Pirates!

402
00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.620
You forget, I'm
Captain Whitebeard.

403
00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.720
Captain, it's time for
your medicine again.

404
00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:37.430
I've got all the
medicine I need right here!

405
00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:39.600
Now silence! Fetch
me another keg!

406
00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:43.240
I hope you know my boss will
hear about all of this!

407
00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.340
Don't make me laugh.

408
00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.440
Anyway, I already have
a pretty good idea

409
00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:48.940
of what the letter's about.

410
00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:52.660
He's worried about
Blackbeard and that kid Ace.

411
00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:54.530
Tell Shanks that if
he wants to talk,

412
00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:57.300
he can come see me himself.

413
00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.600
Now, why don't you take off?

414
00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:03.770
I'm too busy to talk to
a snot‐nosed rookie.

415
00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.940
Run home to your boss.

416
00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:14.920
<b>Edward Newgate
The Great Pirate "Whitebeard"
Strongest Man in the World</b>

417
00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:21.890
<b>A Winter Island</b>

418
00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.260
The old man
hasn't changed a bit.

419
00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:21.890
How are you
laughing at this, boss?

420
00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:27.280
I figured that would happen.
Don't worry about it.

421
00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:29.350
Just give me
a little bit more time.

422
00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:31.940
I promise, I can
straighten this guy out.

423
00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:33.670
I don't know what you
planned to do, my friend,

424
00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:35.860
but forget about it.

425
00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:37.280
You did a good job.

426
00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.480
Now just get yourself
back to base, all right?

427
00:21:40.530 --> 00:21:41.900
B‐But what about my pride?

428
00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:43.890
I have to show
this guy who I am!

429
00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.660
Hey, your life is more important
to me than your pride.

430
00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:48.930
Come on, there's nothin' more
for you to do out there.

431
00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.340
And we have some things to plan.

432
00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:55.780
So, what're we
going to do, boss?

433
00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:58.580
We're going. Prepare
to set sail, men!

434
00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:00.750
You're going to see Whitebeard?

435
00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:01.760
Sure am.

436
00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:03.800
Even you can't think the
government won't react

437
00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:05.930
if you pull a stunt like that.

438
00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:08.870
No, Beckman,
I fully expect them to.

439
00:22:09.900 --> 00:22:12.630
I just don't care.

440
00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.960
Now's not the time to worry
about the government.

441
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:19.000
Before much longer, they'll be
the ones worrying about us.

442
00:22:19.030 --> 00:22:21.840
You heard him, men.
Let's get goin'!

443
00:22:21.870 --> 00:22:26.070
All right, boys. Let's get some
grog ready to take with us.

444
00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:29.290
Teach?

445
00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:30.950
That's right.

446
00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:33.920
He's the captain of the pirate
crew to which I belong.

447
00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:35.790
Tell me, if I've
never heard of him,

448
00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:37.320
what use is he to me?

449
00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:39.920
With no reputation,
he would pose no threat.

450
00:22:40.110 --> 00:22:43.480
You know, I thought
you might feel that way.

451
00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:46.450
And I assure you, we need
only a little bit more time.

452
00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:47.880
We are drawing up a
plan at the moment

453
00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:49.680
that should take
care of everything.

454
00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:52.990
Well, he's
caught my interest anyway.

455
00:22:53.020 --> 00:22:55.330
Why don't we give
him a try, Admiral?

456
00:22:56.550 --> 00:22:59.820
The crew I belong to is known
as the Blackbeard Pirates.

457
00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:02.790
I suggest that you
remember that name.

458
00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:08.760
Hey, did you hear?

459
00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:10.350
Someone beat up Bellamy earlier!

460
00:23:10.380 --> 00:23:12.520
What? Who could do that?

461
00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:19.670
This kid looked too bright‐eyed

462
00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:21.780
to even be worth 30 million.

463
00:23:21.820 --> 00:23:23.800
But 100 million?

464
00:23:23.810 --> 00:23:26.130
So what's our next
move, Captain?

465
00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:30.490
The kid just got lucky...
he's not really worth that much.

466
00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:33.130
Why don't you throw that away
before I do it for you?

467
00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:35.030
That's enough outta you!

468
00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:43.800
Well, that oughta shut him up.

469
00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:46.880
I was looking for someone with a
bounty that was worth my time.

470
00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:51.820
The crew's going to be rich
soon, boys. Very stinkin' rich.

471
00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:53.240
That's what I wanted to hear!

472
00:23:53.290 --> 00:23:56.730
It's about time that we all
had full pockets again.

473
00:23:57.800 --> 00:23:58.830
Hey, Captain!

474
00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:01.240
Weren't we meeting up
with Laffitte in Mock Town?

475
00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:03.870
I haven't seen him
around anywhere.

476
00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:06.840
<b>"Champion" Jesus Burgess
Helmsman, Blackbeard Pirates</b>

477
00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:08.940
Guess we'll just have
to leave without him.

478
00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:11.650
We can't let a bounty
like that get away.

479
00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:13.780
Am I right, Augur?

480
00:24:15.230 --> 00:24:18.810
<b>Marshall D. "Blackbeard" Teach
Captain, Blackbeard Pirates</b>

481
00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:24.780
<b>"Supersonic" Van Augur
Marksman, Blackbeard Pirates</b>

482
00:24:24.890 --> 00:24:28.130
Good Idea. We gotta do all
the livin' we can right now.

483
00:24:28.160 --> 00:24:31.700
Death comes for everyone
some time, even pirates.

484
00:24:30.820 --> 00:24:34.790
<b>Doc Q "the Reaper"
Doctor, Blackbeard Pirates</b>
